      "description": "Watch Philadelphia Union vs Atlanta United FC highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 2, 2026. Football fans witnessed an unforgettable spectacle as tactical shifts and sheer willpower dictated the flow of this intense encounter. The match between Philadelphia Union and Atlanta United , played on August 2, 2026 , delivered a narrative that kept everyone on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. Early Red Card and Atlanta's Resilience The MLS clash ignited in the 26th minute when Atlanta United defender Enea Mihaj was shown a straight red card. Despite heavy protests from his teammates, the visitors were forced to play with ten men for the remainder of the contest. Remarkably, the numerical disadvantage didn't stop Atlanta from striking first. In the 30th minute, Miguel Almiron found the back of the net to give the visitors a shocking 1-0 lead, a scoreline they managed to defend stubbornly heading into the half-time break. Expanding the Lead and the Union's Lifeline The second half began with Atlanta United continuing to defy the odds. In the 66th minute, Tristan Muyumba doubled the lead after a well-placed assist from Aleksey Miranchuk , making it 0-2. The home side, however, began to ramp up the pressure as substitutions changed the dynamic of the game. Philadelphia Union finally broke through in the 73rd minute when Milan Iloski scored to make it 1-2, setting the stage for a grandstand finish as the game moved into a frantic period of stoppage time. The Stoppage-Time Miracle As the clock ticked deep into added time, the Philadelphia Union completed a turnaround for the ages. In the 90+6th minute, Kai Wagner provided a perfect delivery for Neil Pierre to equalize. Before Atlanta could even process the loss of their lead, the Union struck again in the 90+7th minute. Kai Wagner was once again the provider, setting up Ezekiel Alladoh for the winning goal. The stadium erupted as Philadelphia turned a 1-2 deficit into a 3-2 victory in the space of a single minute, capping off a night of pure footballing drama."
